From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 05:08:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 5: career recommendation engine, skill-gap analysis,
 evaluation

- src/recommendation/profiles.py, build_career_skills.py: career skill profiles
  (frequency, importance, low_sample) -> data/processed/career_skills.csv
- src/recommendation/engine.py: weighted_coverage_v1 plus three baselines
  (popularity, keyword overlap, TF-IDF cosine); evidence, tie flags,
  prerequisite-aware gap analysis
- src/recommendation/recommend.py: CLI, stores model_version and created_at,
  --expect-top gate (demo profile ranks Data Analyst first)
- src/evaluation/recommendation_eval.py: Hit@1/3, MRR, P/R/NDCG@3 on gold
  profiles and leave-one-out postings
- data/reference: demo_profile.json, skill_prerequisites.csv (authored, needs review)
- data/evaluation/profile_gold_dev.csv (13 author-written profiles)
- database: curated.career_skills (profile/recommendation tables deferred to Phase 7)
- tests/test_phase5_recommendation.py (3 tests), docs/phase5_recommendation.md

Evaluation is circular on synthetic data; the engine does not beat the TF-IDF baseline.
